# E030: DuplicateKey at eval time — a varref key resolves to the same string as a literal key.
# The parser allows this because $k and "x" look syntactically distinct;
# the duplicate is only detected when $k is evaluated to "x" at runtime.
[k: "x"
 result: [$k: 1  "x": 2]]
=== out
[E030] duplicate key: x
